# Shell scripts are scp'd from a Windows working tree straight to the VPS and
# executed there. A CRLF checkout makes bash read `set -euo pipefail\r` and die
# on line 2 -- which, for monitoring/check-services.sh, means the monitor is
# silently dead and an outage produces NO alert. A broken monitor and a healthy
# system look identical from the outside.
#
# core.autocrlf=input already keeps the committed blobs LF; this makes the
# WORKING TREE LF too, which is what actually gets copied.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by Linux daemons, not by an editor on Windows.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
